# The take at the walked root with one letter (FABLE-OPUS-ROOT-TAKE-20260925-179): R0's inbox holds
# the host's mainArgs letter, so `receiveMessage: m` takes it -- the walker's take primitive stores
# the letter's graph in m's pointer cell -- and m != 0 holds: Entry 1.  (The letter's payload has no
# number to read at the root yet: it holds mainArgs, an Array.)
receiveMessage: m
int: r 0
if: m != 0
    r: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
